  "summary": "Mill Valley suspended its Flock Safety ALPR contract and disabled cameras as of Sept. 9, 2026, after the vendor changed terms of use mid-contract, raising concerns about data privacy and the city's ability to enforce safeguards. The city said it still supports ALPR for legitimate law enforcement uses but only with enforceable privacy and civil liberties protections.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "After an automated license plate recognition technology company changed the terms of use midway through a contract, the city of Mill Valley pulled out over concerns about data privacy and the city's ability to enforce safeguards.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "cameras have been disabled as of Sept. 9, and a contract has been suspended with Flock Safety",
      "paragraph_idx": 1
    },
    {
      "quote": "only with enforceable protections for privacy and civil liberties",
